From fd20e5c5466d41abcc36a42ddfc0dd9d7fd94f31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Travis Gilbert <1travisgilbert@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:24:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(shell): measured layout and bounds observation for
 presented native controls

Adds MeasuredLayout, which places children at host-measured bounds and clips
each one, and BoundsObserver, a transparent element that reports its child's
laid-out bounds during prepaint. Button and Checkbox gain on_bounds; Tab is
addressable as a stateful element and exposes root_child; popup menus and
tab bars carry the bounds hooks through. Theorem's IntelliJ presentation uses
these to place Swing-backed controls and probe their geometry.

Ported from 576089a9 onto the v0.7.0 series. v0.7.0 replaced Icon's path
field with IconSource, so an owner-painted image is the IconSource::Image
variant; native menus show an in-memory ImageSource::Image and omit other
image sources. Docs moved with website/docs/components to website/component.
